Package: litemon
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 systemd
Description: Lightweight local historical system monitor
 LiteMon is a local-first Qt 6 monitor for Linux desktops.
 It records CPU, memory, storage, network, battery, Intel GPU
 and NVIDIA GPU history into a bounded SQLite database,
 with compact charts and a sidebar-driven UI.
 .
 Features:
  * CPU, memory, disk, network, battery, GPU history
  * Intel GPU (sysfs frequency) and NVIDIA GPU (NVML)
  * Per-core CPU charts, envelope bands for long ranges
  * Auto-pruning of empty samples and no-signal GPUs
  * 60-second minimum sampling, 5-minute aggregation

Package: litemon-collector
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 systemd
Description: LiteMon background metrics collector
 Background daemon that samples system metrics and writes them
 to the LiteMon SQLite database. Runs as a systemd user service.